version: "0.7.0"

date-released: "2026-10-26"

abstract: >
  CPC Validation is the reference validation framework for Constraint Physical
  Computing (CPC), with canonical constraint IR, RC, Digital and FPGA backends,
  independent semantic validation and physical-evidence contracts. Version
  0.7.0 includes RFC-0010 open-system software, CPC-SHOR finite simulations,
  bounded P3/P4 software, N0 pre-physical tooling, and the bounded classical
  UP5K/Pico probability/PRNG milestone for seeded physical oracle records 2,
  68 and 194. Historical RFC-0009 P1 evidence remains a separate lineage.
  Known physical error-path discrepancies remain unresolved. Physical N0
  quantum execution, physical Shor factorization, scalable quantum computing,
  quantum advantage and ASI containment are not demonstrated.

